      "id": "197d5032fa5a285b",
      "category": "technology",
      "title": "MONAILabel 0.8.5 on AMD Instinct™ GPUs: Interactive Medical-Image Annotation",
      "summary": "Behind every well-trained medical imaging model is a painstakingly labeled dataset, and behind that dataset is a human expert drawing contours one slice at a time. MONAILabel exists to make that human faster. Developed by Project MONAI (Medical Open Network for AI), it is a widely used open-source active-learning annotation server for medical imaging. It bridges 3D Slicer, the Open Health Imaging Foundation (OHIF) Viewer, and QuPath to MONAI-powered deep learning models, so radiologists and researchers can label 3D",
      "url": "https://rocm.blogs.amd.com/artificial-intelligence/monailabel-2608/README.html",
